        question: "What is the difference between passive and active mine-drainage treatment?",
        answer: "Passive systems--limestone drains, settling ponds, constructed wetlands--use gravity, chemistry, and biology with no power or operators, suiting remote sites with moderate flows. Active systems dose lime or caustic with mechanical equipment and real-time monitoring, handling high flows and heavy contamination but requiring power, operators, and ongoing funding.",
