        question: "What contaminants are typical at old rail yards?",
        answer: "Petroleum hydrocarbons from fueling and maintenance, lead and other metals from paints and industrial activity, creosote (PAHs) from treated ties, ash and cinder fill with elevated metals, and sometimes chlorinated solvents from maintenance shops. The Phase I assessment identifies which of these a specific site likely has; the Phase II investigation confirms it with sampling.",
